# Backend / Server Engine

## Choosing the server
- **Inside Next.js** (route handlers, server actions): simple CRUD for the site/admin, forms, auth callbacks.
- **Separate server engine** when there is a mobile app, heavy business logic, background jobs, public API,
  WhatsApp/AI processing, or multiple clients. Choose:
  - **Node.js — NestJS** (default; shares TypeScript types with Next.js/Expo).
  - **Python — FastAPI** when the core is data/AI/ML heavy or needs Python libraries. Record in an ADR.

## Node.js (NestJS) layout
```
src/modules/<domain>/  <domain>.module.ts · controller · service · repository · dto/ · jobs/ · *.spec.ts
src/common/            guards, interceptors, filters, decorators, config
```
Controllers: HTTP only. Services: business logic, no HTTP objects. Global `ValidationPipe({ whitelist, forbidNonWhitelisted, transform })`.

## Python (FastAPI) layout
```
app/
  main.py               app factory, middleware, routers
  core/                 config (pydantic-settings), security, logging
  api/v1/<domain>.py    routers (HTTP only)
  services/<domain>.py  business logic
  repositories/         SQLAlchemy 2.x (async) data access
  models/ · schemas/    ORM models · Pydantic v2 schemas
  workers/              background jobs (arq / Celery / RQ on Redis)
migrations/             Alembic
tests/                  pytest (+ httpx AsyncClient)
pyproject.toml          uv or poetry; ruff + mypy configured
```
Type hints everywhere, `mypy --strict` on new modules, `ruff` lint + format.

## API conventions (both)
- REST, versioned `/api/v1/...`, plural kebab-case resources. OpenAPI kept accurate (protected in production).
- Validate every input; reject unknown fields.
- Paginated lists (`limit` ≤ 100 or cursor) returning `{ data, meta }`.
- One error shape: `{ "error": { "code", "message", "details", "requestId" } }`; correct status codes.
- `Idempotency-Key` supported on payments, messaging and other non-repeatable POSTs.

## Config
Validated config at startup (zod/joi or pydantic-settings); fail fast on missing variables. Read env only in the config module.

## Background work
Slow, external or retryable work (WhatsApp/email sends, AI calls, webhook processing, imports/exports, reports)
runs in a queue on Redis (BullMQ / arq / Celery): idempotent, retries with backoff, `tenantId` in payload,
failed jobs monitored.

## Logging & observability
Structured JSON logs with `requestId`, `tenantId`, `userId` — never PII or secrets. `/health/live` and
`/health/ready` (DB + Redis). Errors to Sentry with environment tag.

## Code basics
Strict typing; no unexplained `any`/`# type: ignore`. Store time in UTC, display `Asia/Jerusalem`.
Money as integer agorot or `numeric` — never float.
